From 5a07018b2a0c01fafb427f817320374f80f645fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotlouis <1891109+dotlouis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:19:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/41] MTROPOLIS: Draw elements rotated by the Thereware
 Rotator

The Rotator only stored its angle, so nothing turned on screen. The
element of a Rotator is as large as the bounds of its rotated image, and
the image was stretched to fill it, which made the zodiac discs of the
Istanbul page in Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage far too large.

Image and mToon elements with a Rotator now draw their contents at their
own size, centered in the element, and rotated by the Rotator angle
around the element center moved by the new "axisoffset" attribute. The
rotated image is cached until the angle, the axis or the contents
change. The Istanbul cover swings open around an axis offset this way.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
